enables → F2, F5; addresses → HV-04.

= Technology Option - Local server, one instance per resident (selected) [TECH-04] =

**Report Format:** §1.3 Technology

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|TECH-04
|Name|Local server, one instance per resident (selected)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Group reasoning. Care homes already run local networks and work phones.
|Category|AI/ICT
|Capabilities|(((
* One instance per resident, in its own encrypted store: profile, own-word list, settings (RP-02), consent register
* The relationship map (TECH-05)
* Staff alerts to work phones over the home's Wi-Fi
* Session record (F6)
* No internet connection; updates by signed package, installed on site
)))
|Limitations|A single point of failure. No remote maintenance. Backups on site.
|Maturity and feasibility|High; standard parts. Run by ST-07.
|Failure and fallback behaviour|Server down: no alerts and no personal starters, so walks run as today. Staff see the state at the start.
|Benefits|HV-03: nothing leaves the home. HV-01: each resident's own settings.
|Drawbacks|Maintenance load on ST-07.
|Selected or rejected|Selected.

== Graph edges ==

enables → F1, F4, F5, F6; addresses → HV-01, HV-03.

= Technology Option - Exchange between instances (selected) [TECH-05] =

**Report Format:** §1.3 Technology

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|TECH-05
|Name|Exchange between instances (selected)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Group reasoning.
|Category|AI/ICT
|Capabilities|(((
For one walk, two residents' instances exchange a list of shareable items. An item is offered only if:

1. its owner said yes to it, privately, before this walk
1. the relationship map allows it for this pair
1. it is off-limits for neither resident in this pair

Unknown pair, or a map change awaiting review: nothing exchanged. Items deleted at the end of the walk. Audit: item IDs only.

Relationship map, per resident: sensitive topics, each with trusted persons and the agreed approach. Per pair: walk agreed (both, date); off-limits topics; shareable items; "again" or "not again" after each walk. Kept by ST-05 with ST-04 and family; reviewed after any death, diagnosis, conflict or move, before the next walk.
)))
|Limitations|The map is only as current as staff keep it. Residents can still tell each other secrets themselves.
|Maturity and feasibility|Medium; simple rules, careful upkeep.
|Failure and fallback behaviour|Exchange fails: no personal starters; place cues only.
|Benefits|HV-06: common ground. HV-03: secrets kept.
|Drawbacks|Strains VT-04. Upkeep for ST-05.
|Selected or rejected|Selected.

== Graph edges ==

enables → F1, F2, F4; addresses → HV-03, HV-06; strains → VT-04.

= Technology Option - Walker model and starters (selected) [TECH-06] =

**Report Format:** §1.3 Technology

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|TECH-06
|Name|Walker model and starters (selected)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Group reasoning; HFC-03 to HFC-05. Offline speech recognition exists for Dutch (e.g. Vosk, whisper.cpp); accuracy for older speakers is lower (Vipperla et al., 2010).
|Category|AI/ICT
|Capabilities|(((
Per walker, for one walk:

* Topics: keywords matched to the person's own-word list
* Stories told this walk: keyword overlap
* Pause type: mid-sentence or finished, from pitch and filler words
* Sensitive topics: keywords from the map

Sentences from prepared, checked templates and lines ("[Name] was telling you about [topic]"); no free text generation. Learns the person's words and dialect if allowed. Transcript and thread deleted at the end of the walk.
)))
|Limitations|Keywords miss meaning. State inference is crude; the listener's codes check it (M-01).
|Maturity and feasibility|Medium. Recognition accuracy is the main risk (O-3).
|Failure and fallback behaviour|Low confidence: wait and place cues only; no thread echo.
|Benefits|HV-02, HV-06, HV-07.
|Drawbacks|Strains VT-05.
|Selected or rejected|Selected.

== Graph edges ==

enables → F2, F4; addresses → HV-02, HV-06, HV-07; strains → VT-05.

= Technology Option - Cloud speech and language services (rejected) [TECH-07] =

**Report Format:** §1.3 Technology

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|TECH-07
|Name|Cloud speech and language services (rejected)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Group reasoning.
|Category|AI/ICT
|Capabilities|Better recognition; free conversation; generated starters.
|Limitations|Needs an internet connection.
|Maturity and feasibility|High.
|Failure and fallback behaviour|Not applicable - rejected.
|Benefits|Understands more; says more.
|Drawbacks|Conversations leave the home (HV-03). A generated sentence can be untrue about a person's own life, and cannot be checked before it is said (HV-08).
|Selected or rejected|Rejected.

